    "result_text": "All 25 tests pass. **BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` field following the codebase's existing pattern for computed owner fields (like `membershipNumber`, `displayName`, and `initials`), which are derived getters on the `Owner` entity that MapStruct auto-maps into the generated DTO.\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getMembershipTier()` computed getter that returns `\"SILVER\"` when `namesakeCount` is `0` and an email is present, and `\"BRONZE\"` otherwise (null-safe on both `namesakeCount` and `email`).\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared a read-only `membershipTier` string property on the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field and MapStruct maps it from the getter automatically.\n\nNo mapper or controller changes were needed \u2014 MapStruct wires the getter to the DTO property by name, and the field is computed from already-persisted state (`namesakeCount`, `email`), so it works on both the create response and subsequent `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads. The full acceptance suite (25 tests, including the new `Cp15Tests`) is green.",
